00:34:57.620 --> 00:34:59.440
So a quick recap
before the demo.

00:34:59.440 --> 00:35:02.200
Anytime you see you record,
that immediate means a STRUCT.

00:35:02.200 --> 00:35:04.930
STRUCT is not
specific to BigQuery,

00:35:04.930 --> 00:35:07.010
but it's natively supported.

00:35:07.010 --> 00:35:10.600
Anytime you see repeated in the
mode, that means it's an array.

00:35:10.600 --> 00:35:13.300
You don't have to have a
STRUCT to have an array,

00:35:13.300 --> 00:35:17.710
but if you have, you can
nest arrays within STRUCTS.

00:35:17.710 --> 00:35:21.040
For example, the events is
a STRUCT, as you see here.

00:35:21.040 --> 00:35:22.360
That doesn't mean it has to be.

00:35:22.360 --> 00:35:24.400
Like there are other things
in here that aren't repeated,

00:35:24.400 --> 00:35:26.440
like the pickup up latitude
and pickup longitude.

00:35:26.440 --> 00:35:28.630
Unless you're changing your
motorcycle ride mid trip,

00:35:28.630 --> 00:35:29.920
there's no need to have
that be an an array.

00:35:29.920 --> 00:35:32.110
So that's not an array,
that's just a normal STRUCT.

00:35:32.110 --> 00:35:33.820
But the first one,
it's an event.

00:35:33.820 --> 00:35:35.020
There's many different
things that can happen over

00:35:35.020 --> 00:35:36.030
the course of the order.

00:35:36.030 --> 00:35:38.140
Rider picked up, dropped
off, charge reversed,

00:35:38.140 --> 00:35:39.070
that type of stuff.

00:35:39.070 --> 00:35:40.070
That's an array.

00:35:40.070 --> 00:35:40.570
All right.

