00:46:27.480 --> 00:46:29.230
Again, you're going
to get back something.

00:46:29.230 --> 00:46:31.710
BigQuery is going to say,
hey, remember that talk?

00:46:31.710 --> 00:46:34.430
Hopefully you didn't
sleep through it.

00:46:34.430 --> 00:46:36.650
It's going to give
you back, for example

00:46:36.650 --> 00:46:40.040
this problem is whether or not a
visitor who visits your website

00:46:40.040 --> 00:46:41.938
is going to buy or not
buy on a return visit.

00:46:41.938 --> 00:46:43.730
It could be whatever
problem that you want.

00:46:43.730 --> 00:46:46.340
But for a classification
model, each of those classes,

00:46:46.340 --> 00:46:48.500
yes they will buy,
no they won't buy,

00:46:48.500 --> 00:46:50.420
is going to return
back in an array.

00:46:50.420 --> 00:46:54.110
And it's going to give you
a confidence, 55% I'm sure,

00:46:54.110 --> 00:46:58.912
44% I'm not sure, and again,
what's the main, huge--

00:46:58.912 --> 00:47:01.370
if you're working with arrays,
as soon as you see that word

00:47:01.370 --> 00:47:03.370
array inside of BigQuery,
what's that other word

00:47:03.370 --> 00:47:05.970
it starts with a U that you
should immediately memorize?

00:47:05.970 --> 00:47:06.890
UNNEST.

00:47:06.890 --> 00:47:09.410
That's exactly what I'm going
to do in the last piece here,

00:47:09.410 --> 00:47:11.760
and then we'll open
it up for questions.

00:47:11.760 --> 00:47:15.500
So this is the example of the
final, final result, where

00:47:15.500 --> 00:47:17.645
you can do cool things like--

00:47:17.645 --> 00:47:19.020
I want the machine
learning model

00:47:19.020 --> 00:47:20.510
